    "text": "The three steps in this phase are as follows. Step-1: The client sends the first segment, a SYN segment, in which only the SYN flag Is set. > This segment is for synchronization of sequence numbers. > It consumes one sequence number. > is the data transfer starts, the sequence number is incremented by 1. A SYN segment cannot carry data} but it consumes one sequence number. Step-2: The server sends second segment, a SYN +ACK segment, with 2 flag bits set: SYN and ACK. > ItisaSYN segment for communication in other direction and serves as the ack for the SYN. > It consumes one sequence number. SYN +ACK segment cannot carry data, but consume one sequence number.",
